272
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:27,280
Keep her by your side, huh?

273
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,280
I'll do what I can.

274
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:30,280
Not so hard. We still have lunch tomorrow.

275
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:31,280
Not so hard enough to skip a free one.

276
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:32,280
Probably at one o'clock, huh?

277
00:12:32,280 --> 00:12:33,280
Yeah, we'll tee off at two.

278
00:12:33,280 --> 00:12:34,280
Right. Good night.

279
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:35,280
Good night.

280
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:37,280
Yeah, tee off on this, Oscar Goldman.

281
00:12:37,280 --> 00:12:44,280
It's the 20th hour of the telethon, ladies and gentlemen, and we're halfway to our goal.

282
00:12:44,280 --> 00:12:48,280
Now to put on some pampers and watch Flower Drum Song.

283
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:53,280
Ah, good night, Ann.

284
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:57,280
Smells like Elvis in there.

285
00:12:57,280 --> 00:13:03,280
Good to see the senator keeping up with the issues.

286
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:05,280
Sweeney Todd.

287
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:08,280
It's a very dangerous toothbrush.

288
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:09,280
Oh.

289
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:11,280
Hi, guy.

290
00:13:11,280 --> 00:13:12,280
Oh, no.

291
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:16,280
We've got to find out more about this Russia thing.

292
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:21,280
Pookie Nuts is in trouble.

293
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:24,280
They made nasolabial troughs much bigger back then.

294
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:29,280
Did my fireplace make that noise?

295
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:32,280
Maybe my couch made that noise.

296
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:34,280
It could be the lamp.

297
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:35,280
Maybe my wife's portrait.

298
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:36,280
No, no.

299
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:39,280
We're about to see a political career come to a screeching halt.

300
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:42,280
Did Johnny Hodges let himself in?

301
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:48,280
Tong, did you meow?

302
00:13:50,280 --> 00:13:51,280
No.

303
00:13:51,280 --> 00:13:57,280
Oh, Ann, you dropped a stuffed animal.

304
00:13:57,280 --> 00:14:00,280
This is going to be much better than pancakes.

305
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:05,280
This to me is the very definition of getting lucky.

306
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:07,280
No, no, don't.

307
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:08,280
What?

308
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:09,280
I waxed.

309
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:10,280
I'm sorry.

310
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:11,280
I wasn't doing anything.

311
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:12,280
I mean nothing wrong.

312
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:13,280
I didn't take anything.

313
00:14:13,280 --> 00:14:14,280
I'm sure of it.

314
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:17,280
You must have the clearest conscience in San Diego to sleep like that.

315
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:18,280
Or were you sleeping?

316
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:20,280
Oh, I was pushed. Please don't get mad.

317
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:21,280
I already am.

318
00:14:21,280 --> 00:14:24,280
Now before I pick up that phone, I want to know two things.

319
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:25,280
Who are you and who put you up to this?

320
00:14:25,280 --> 00:14:26,280
And will you kiss me?

321
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:27,280
Put me up to it.

322
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:28,280
You need time on that, huh?

323
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:30,280
All right, start with the easy part, your name.

324
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:32,280
You do know your name.

325
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:33,280
Kitten W. Whip.

326
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:34,280
Jody?

327
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:36,280
Jody Drew?

328
00:14:36,280 --> 00:14:38,280
Oh, I can't stay mad.

329
00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:39,280
Well, that's why I call myself.

330
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:40,280
Very creative.

331
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:41,280
Another one you were born with.

332
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:43,280
Stanley Myron Handelman.

333
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:44,280
I don't use it, so why should you?

334
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:46,280
And besides, what's yours?

335
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:47,280
Oh, you wouldn't know.

336
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:49,280
You wouldn't know about the Stratton shipping lines.

337
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:50,280
That's right, mister.

338
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:52,280
I don't know a thing about you, and I don't know what you're trying to make of all this.

339
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:53,280
You're large, is that it?

340
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:54,280
You walk in your sleep.

341
00:14:54,280 --> 00:14:56,280
You just happened to wake up in the wrong bed.

342
00:14:56,280 --> 00:14:58,280
Or maybe you're expecting someone.

343
00:14:58,280 --> 00:15:01,280
An indignant father, an outraged husband, a few photographers.

344
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:02,280
What if they get lost too?

345
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:03,280
I'm alone.

346
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:04,280
Is that what you think?

347
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:05,280
There's nobody else.

348
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:06,280
Oh, this is David Stratton.

349
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,280
Has Lieutenant Woodman come in yet?

350
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:09,280
He's with Mr. Carter, sir.

351
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:13,280
Let go of my ego.

352
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:16,280
I think Senator Kennedy might have handled this differently.

353
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:18,280
The VC kept coming.

354
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:20,280
I couldn't keep him off me.

355
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:22,280
No, don't do that.

356
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:23,280
Stop it.

357
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:24,280
I can see your roots.

358
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:25,280
It's no good.

359
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:26,280
It doesn't help.

360
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:29,280
I mean, it helps, but it's just not very convincing.

361
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:31,280
Right.

362
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:32,280
Right the first time.

363
00:15:32,280 --> 00:15:33,280
I bet you're always right.

364
00:15:33,280 --> 00:15:35,280
Go ahead and make your car.

365
00:15:35,280 --> 00:15:36,280
I don't even care anymore.

366
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:45,280
Where is everybody?

367
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:46,280
Your wife, the little girl?

368
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:48,280
They're out of town.

369
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:49,280
But let's stick to your story.

370
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:51,280
Okay, I'm going to pack.

371
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:53,280
But it's all so silly.

372
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:57,280
And if my parents ever found out why they yanked me out of college on the spot,

373
00:15:57,280 --> 00:15:59,280
well, they're terribly strict, terribly proper.

374
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:01,280
They'd never understand.

375
00:16:01,280 --> 00:16:03,280
I mean, you know, these sorority initiates.

376
00:16:03,280 --> 00:16:05,280
In the middle of summer.

377
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:08,280
Well, we're on a four-master system thing where they're thinking...

378
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:10,280
Let's call these terribly strict, terribly proper parents.

379
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:11,280
No.

380
00:16:11,280 --> 00:16:12,280
No way.

381
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:13,280
Oh, is that it?

382
00:16:13,280 --> 00:16:14,280
Trouble at home.

383
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:15,280
Yes, but will you listen?

384
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:16,280
If you'll tell it.

385
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:18,280
Alright.

386
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:19,280
Here's my pitch.

387
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:20,280
Alright.

388
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:21,280
I'm a Martian with the CIA.

389
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:23,280
Like you said, I was running.

390
00:16:23,280 --> 00:16:24,280
Running away.

391
00:16:24,280 --> 00:16:25,280
Yeah.

392
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:26,280
I found your front door open a crack?

393
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:28,280
No, that's another lie.

394
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:29,280
Oh.

395
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:31,280
I set the one to screen next to the back door,

396
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:33,280
breaking and entering, 90 days next case.

397
00:16:33,280 --> 00:16:35,280
Running from what, your parents?

398
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:36,280
Parents.

399
00:16:36,280 --> 00:16:37,280
My parents were mangs.

400
00:16:37,280 --> 00:16:39,280
I never knew who my old man was,

401
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:41,280
and I doubt if dear old mom does either.

402
00:16:41,280 --> 00:16:43,280
No, it was Barney, Barney the slob.

403
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:44,280
One of her gentleman callers.

404
00:16:44,280 --> 00:16:46,280
That's who I was running from.

405
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:49,280
Oh, I should have taken off years ago.

406
00:16:49,280 --> 00:16:50,280
What happened last night?

407
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:52,280
I got to bed, but not to sleep.

408
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:53,280
Too much furniture falling down,

409
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:55,280
and too much of them doing the same.

410
00:16:55,280 --> 00:16:56,280
See, they're acrobats.

411
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:58,280
I guess mother was taken unconscious.

412
00:16:58,280 --> 00:17:00,280
She isn't too terribly strong.

413
00:17:00,280 --> 00:17:03,280
Sorry, I put the emphasis on the wrong word there.

414
00:17:03,280 --> 00:17:05,280
Then Barney stumbled into my room.

415
00:17:05,280 --> 00:17:06,280
Baby bop too.

416
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,280
Looking for a live one.

417
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:09,280
What is this live one?

418
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:11,280
You follow all this?

419
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:12,280
You live behind walls here, man.

420
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:14,280
Where I come from is outer space.

421
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:16,280
Men are from Mars, women are from Venus, right?

422
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:17,280
Well, before I knew it, he was all over me,

423
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:18,280
but I got a knee up,

424
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:20,280
and it was almost worth it to hear him howl.

425
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:22,280
I made a die for the door, but he grabbed me.

426
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:23,280
I guess he would have killed me,

427
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:25,280
only I'm sort of slobbering myself.

428
00:17:25,280 --> 00:17:27,280
I made it out the window.

429
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:30,280
I'm sorry, a little bit of the king slipped out there.

430
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:33,280
Man, how I got this far, I'll never know.

431
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:37,280
Perhaps it was your pert acting ability.

432
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:38,280
He did this.

433
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:39,280
Gave you a booster shot?

434
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:41,280
Oh.

435
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:44,280
You want to trade '90s or...

436
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:48,280
All I've been thinking about is the damage you might be doing me.

437
00:17:48,280 --> 00:17:50,280
Well, that's not all I was thinking about.

438
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:51,280
I'm sorry.

439
00:17:51,280 --> 00:17:53,280
You mean it?

440
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,280
You won't make me go back?

441
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:55,280
To that?

442
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:57,280
You won't make me go back?

443
00:17:57,280 --> 00:17:58,280
But you'll need help.

444
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:00,280
By the juvenile authorities.

445
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:02,280
We've met.

446
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:05,280
They'll either send me back or put me away.

447
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:07,280
Now, what's the difference?

448
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:08,280
That's the Jodie doll.

449
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:12,280
You wind her up and any way you point her, she turns up lousy.

450
00:18:12,280 --> 00:18:13,280
No, no, no.

451
00:18:13,280 --> 00:18:14,280
No, no, no, no.

452
00:18:14,280 --> 00:18:16,280
We'll think of something.

453
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:17,280
Oui?

454
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:18,280
Oui.

455
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:21,280
The Gestapo!

456
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:25,280
Oh, no, she's marking the couch.

457
00:18:25,280 --> 00:18:27,280
Sure, fine, I'll get it.

458
00:18:27,280 --> 00:18:31,280
I always have to get the damn door.

459
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:33,280
Well, good morning, Martha.

460
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:34,280
Oh, I hope I didn't get you off.

461
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:36,280
No, no, no, I was just...

462
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:38,280
Have you taken on the paper route?

463
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:39,280
Oh, these.

464
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:41,280
That's why I stopped.

465
00:18:41,280 --> 00:18:43,280
They were scattered all over your front lawn.

466
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:44,280
Six days.

467
00:18:44,280 --> 00:18:47,280
You know, the police say that's like an open invitation to burglars.

468
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:48,280
So here I am.

469
00:18:48,280 --> 00:18:49,280
I heard that, yes.

470
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:51,280
I'll have to be more careful.

471
00:18:51,280 --> 00:18:54,280
Working late and leaving early, coming and going through the garage.

472
00:18:54,280 --> 00:18:55,280
I just never noticed them.

473
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:56,280
So bye now.

474
00:18:56,280 --> 00:18:57,280
No harm done.

475
00:18:57,280 --> 00:18:58,280
Okay, bye.

476
00:18:58,280 --> 00:18:59,280
Well, what did you hear from my little sister?

477
00:18:59,280 --> 00:19:00,280
Nothing.

478
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:01,280
Goodbye now.

479
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:02,280
Oh, she's fine.

480
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:03,280
Kathy's fine.

481
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:04,280
Everything's fine.

482
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:05,280
Fine, bye now.

483
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:06,280
I expect them back soon.

484
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:08,280
I'm not quite sure of the date.

485
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:09,280
Yeah, goodbye.

486
00:19:09,280 --> 00:19:10,280
You'll be the first to know.

487
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:11,280
Bye.

488
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:12,280
Oh, David, I hope you don't think I'm checking up on you.

489
00:19:12,280 --> 00:19:13,280
I just have to come by.

490
00:19:13,280 --> 00:19:14,280
Oh, no, bye.

491
00:19:14,280 --> 00:19:15,280
No, no, it was very considerate.

492
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:16,280
Okay, see you.

493
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:17,280
I'm sorry I'm not dressed.

494
00:19:17,280 --> 00:19:18,280
Oh, I couldn't stay in any case.

495
00:19:18,280 --> 00:19:19,280
Good, bye.

496
00:19:19,280 --> 00:19:20,280
Unless there's something that...

497
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:22,280
I'll hold the fort or send up a flare.

498
00:19:22,280 --> 00:19:23,280
Yeah, bye.

499
00:19:23,280 --> 00:19:24,280
Okay.

500
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:26,280
Well, don't hesitate, dear, if there's anything at all.

501
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:28,280
Look, I've got a girl in the oven.

502
00:19:28,280 --> 00:19:29,280
You do.

503
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:30,280
Thanks again.

504
00:19:30,280 --> 00:19:31,280
Copper-bottomed old...

505
00:19:31,280 --> 00:19:32,280
Goodbye.

506
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:35,280
Last night when you were running.

507
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:36,280
Was it sensuous?

508
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:38,280
You must have had some idea where you were going.

509
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:42,280
Mm, I've got this sort of aunt, you know, up in L.A.

510
00:19:42,280 --> 00:19:43,280
Carpenter aunt lives in a trunk of wood.

511
00:19:43,280 --> 00:19:44,280
She wanted to talk to my mother.

512
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:46,280
I guess she put me up all right.

513
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:49,280
Though I must admit, I like it better here.

514
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:51,280
Well, you can't stay here.

515
00:19:51,280 --> 00:19:52,280
What am I...

516
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:53,280
Of course you can stay here.

517
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:54,280
You can't just leave.

518
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:55,280
Not like that.

519
00:19:55,280 --> 00:19:57,280
How long have these been here?

520
00:19:57,280 --> 00:20:00,280
Well, if I could borrow something,

521
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:02,280
I could mail it back for my aunts.

522
00:20:02,280 --> 00:20:06,280
Maybe your wife's got some old thing she's ready to throw away.

523
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:07,280
Aside from me.

524
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:10,280
As long as I've known her, she's never thrown a thing away.

525
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:13,280
Anyway, she's not your size.

526
00:20:13,280 --> 00:20:14,280
What size is she?

527
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:15,280
Seven.

528
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:16,280
This way, please.

529
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:17,280
Well, let me show you something

530
00:20:17,280 --> 00:20:19,280
in the Ruth Buzzy line of leather and PVC.

531
00:20:19,280 --> 00:20:21,280
These are the sevens.

532
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:22,280
Any particular color?

533
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:24,280
Oh, just something cool.

534
00:20:24,280 --> 00:20:25,280
Transparent.

535
00:20:25,280 --> 00:20:26,280
This one, maybe.

536
00:20:26,280 --> 00:20:27,280
Mm, very nice.

537
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:28,280
I would go slip it up.

538
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:29,280
Practition two.

539
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:30,280
Drip dry.

540
00:20:30,280 --> 00:20:31,280
Fine.

541
00:20:31,280 --> 00:20:32,280
Needs no ironing.

542
00:20:32,280 --> 00:20:33,280
Fine, I'll take it.

543
00:20:33,280 --> 00:20:34,280
Whatever.

544
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:35,280
Fine.

545
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:36,280
I'll need some other things, too.

546
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:39,280
You know, some of those filthy things.

547
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:42,280
Might as well give me the mannequin, too.

548
00:20:42,280 --> 00:20:44,280
